
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the values. `.env` is gitignored.

# --- Backend API (all published content) --------------------------------------
# Where the public site reads programs, faculty, alumni, blogs, jobs, policies
# and FAQs from, and where the consultation and enrol forms post their leads.
# This is the connection that makes an admin-panel change appear on the site.
#
# Include the version prefix:  https://api.careerveda.in/api/v1
#
# Left blank, the site runs entirely off its static data files in src/data and
# the forms post to the serverless functions in api/ — the arrangement that
# predates the backend. Nothing breaks; the admin panel simply has no effect on
# what visitors see.
#
# In `npm run dev` this defaults to http://localhost:8080/api/v1, so a locally
# running backend is picked up with no configuration at all.
#
# The backend must list this site's origin in CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS (or
# FRONTEND_URL) or every request is refused by the browser.
VITE_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=
#
# IMPORTANT: Vite inlines every variable prefixed with VITE_ into the JavaScript
# it ships to the browser. Anything secret must NOT have that prefix. The
# variables below are read only by the serverless function in api/, which runs
# on the server, so they never reach a visitor.

# --- MongoDB (consultation + enrollment forms) --------------------------------
# From MongoDB Atlas: Database → Connect → Drivers.
# Looks like: mongodb+srv://user:password@cluster0.abcde.mongodb.net/?retryWrites=true&w=majority
#
# Two collections are written, both by serverless functions in api/:
#   consultations  ← the home page consultation form  (api/consultation.js)
#   enrollments    ← the /enroll application form     (api/enroll.js)
#
# Set the same variable in Vercel → Settings → Environment Variables, or the
# forms return 503 in production.
MONGODB_URI=

# Database name. Optional — defaults to "careerveda" if left blank.
MONGODB_DB=careerveda
